# This site is a single index.html file with client-side routing (no
# separate file exists at /services, /post/some-slug, etc.). Without this
# rule, visiting one of those URLs directly, or refreshing the page while
# on one, would 404 — Netlify has no real file to serve at that path.
#
# This rule says: for any path that doesn't match a real file (Netlify
# always checks for a real file first — this never overrides /admin,
# /images/*, /content/*, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, etc.), serve index.html
# with a 200 status, and let the page's own JavaScript render the right
# view based on the URL.
/*    /index.html   200
